{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #375 [status: falsifiable; formalized: yes]. Is it true that for any $n,k\\geq 1$, if $n+1,\\ldots,n+k$ are all composite then there are distinct primes $p_1,\\ldots,p_k$ such that $p_i\\mid n+i$ for $1\\leq i\\leq k$? Current best: Note this is trivial when $k\\leq 2$. Grimm proved that this is true if $k\\ll \\log n/\\log\\log n$. Erd\\H{o}s and Selfridge improved this to $k\\leq (1+o(1))\\log n$. Ramachandra, Shorey, and Tijdeman \\cite{RST75} have improved this to\\[k\\ll\\left(\\frac{\\log n}{\\log\\log n}\\right)^3.\\]This is problem B32 in Guy's collection \\cite{Gu04}. Prize: no. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_0b8c50e7f85e54458b4cff27bce9f387df9b0280ecf978aabdd76f822bc5330b","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:375","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_51f38920b6c6e358","object_root":"sha256:b55dfa1a8cf1bec8bf6676311ec64729438abb88a4820f1687a671ca9ba43d4d","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"dat